        "text": "def solve(rows):\n    \"\"\"Solves the interval merging problem according to the specified rules.\n\n    Args:\n        rows: A list of tuples, where each tuple represents an interval (start, end).\n\n    Returns:\n        A sorted list of merged intervals.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Audit filter: Omit positions where index modulo 3 equals 0, except for the last position\n    original_positions = list(range(len(rows)))\n    filtered_positions = [pos for pos in original_positions if pos % 3 != 0 or pos == len(rows) - 1]\n    \n    # Rotate the retained rows left by 3 positions modulo the retained length\n    rotated_rows = []\n    for i in filtered_positions:\n        start, end = rows[i]\n        rotated_start = (start + 3) % len(rows) if len(rows) > 0 else 0\n        rotated_end = (end + 3) % len(rows)\n        rotated_rows.append((rotated_start, rotated_end))\n\n    # Apply interval rules\n    merged_intervals = []\n    for start, end in rotated_rows:\n        if start <= end:\n            merged_intervals.append((start, end))\n\n    # Merge overlapping intervals\n    merged_intervals.sort()\n    final_intervals = []\n    if merged_intervals:\n        current_start, current_end = merged_intervals[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(merged_intervals)):\n            next_start, next_end = merged_intervals[i]\n            if next_start <= current_end + 1:\n                current_end = max(current_end, next_end)\n            else:\n                final_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n                current_start, current_end = next_start, next_end\n        final_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n\n    return final_intervals",
